WEBVTT

00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:44.086
Yes?

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.421
Hi, Dad! It's me and my co-workers.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.049
Open up, Leo.
It's Amy and her weirdos.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.970
Howdy, friends! Welcome to Mars!

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.599
Thanks so much for inviting us, Mr. Wong.

00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.726
I've never been to a Mars Day Barbecue.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.104
Oh, Mars Day much better than Earth Day.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:04.898
Dump trash wherever you want.
Big empty planet.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:07.359
Okay, then! Make yourselves at home.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:09.152
Don't mind if I already did.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:13.073
By the way, do you have anymore
of this Dom Perignon Bubble Bath?

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.659
There was only enough
to fill the tub halfway.

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:22.916
This is quite a large ranch you have.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.918
Seventeen-point-nine billion acres.

00:01:25.127 --> 00:01:27.087
We own entire Western Hemisphere.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:28.964
That the best hemisphere.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:30.632
It's the same on Earth.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.888
Here is
most number one product of all.

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:37.347
The mighty Buggalo.

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:38.724
They used for everything.

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:41.393
Meat, milk, and their shells
make good row boat.

00:01:41.894 --> 00:01:43.812
I broke your television!

00:01:44.188 --> 00:01:46.982
Man, it must take forever
to brand all those cattle.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.901
Not really. We own so much stuff,

00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:51.612
it easier just to brand
everything that not ours.

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:55.324
Please don't do that.

00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:59.369
Hey! Betsy!

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.832
This is my sweet little Betsy.

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:06.418
I raised her from a larva
that ate one of my sweaters.

00:02:06.502 --> 00:02:08.253
Yes, everybody love Betsy.

00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:10.005
We going to eat her at Amy's wedding.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:11.715
If she ever get married.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.634
Dad! Gleesh!

00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:16.762
Please don't say things like that
when you meet my boyfriend tonight.

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:17.888
Ah, that right.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.807
We finally get to spend
some time with this Mr. Kiff.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:24.436
I just hope he's a nice man
who can make us lot of grand children.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.689
This not some parallel universe
where you’re getting any younger.

00:02:37.616 --> 00:02:38.700
Now remember, Kiff.

00:02:38.784 --> 00:02:41.828
The quickest way to a girl's bed
is through her parents.

00:02:42.037 --> 00:02:43.705
Have sex with them, and you're in.

00:02:43.789 --> 00:02:48.001
Actually, Sir, I'm... I'm a little
nervous about meeting her family.

00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:51.129
Well, that's natural.
After all, you're meek and uninteresting.

00:02:51.213 --> 00:02:53.924
Until now, you've gotten by
on my leftover charisma.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.593
Scrounging off it,
like a tiny charisma parasite.

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:58.220
I just hope they like me.

00:02:58.345 --> 00:02:59.429
And why wouldn't they?

00:02:59.555 --> 00:03:00.889
Yes, yes, I know.

00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:02.766
Tiny, meek, uninteresting.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.812
Spare me your tedious life story, Kiff.
And above all, have fun!

00:03:11.358 --> 00:03:13.026
Yeah, get on down!

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.782
Oh, yeah! Drop another
barnyard bomb on us, Vanilla Corn!

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:21.785
Yo, fool! It's Mix-Master Festus.

00:03:36.508 --> 00:03:38.260
So what's Mars Day about, anyway?

00:03:38.343 --> 00:03:40.804
It commemorate the day, centuries ago,

00:03:40.888 --> 00:03:45.100
when our ancestor, Sir Reginald Wong,
bought Mars from stupid natives.

00:03:45.184 --> 00:03:47.603
How can you call
the native Martians stupid?

00:03:47.686 --> 00:03:49.688
They sell whole planet for one bead.

00:03:49.771 --> 00:03:50.856
Sound stupid to me.

00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:53.734
That is stupid!

00:03:53.817 --> 00:03:55.611
I can't believe you're laughing

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:58.947
at the tragic exploitation of a proud,
bead loving people.

00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:00.824
Lighten up, Leela. It's funny.

00:04:00.908 --> 00:04:03.410
Of course it is.
But you don't have to laugh!

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:08.999
Amy, no. Not on your parent's planet.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.083
Howdy, Amy.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.169
Glad to see you've come back
to the country.

00:04:12.294 --> 00:04:13.670
It's where the flavor is.

00:04:15.047 --> 00:04:17.174
R.J. this is my boyfriend, Kiff.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.258
This wimp?

00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:20.385
You've gone a long way, baby.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.304
Cigarette, pardner?

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:23.555
Oh, I don't...

00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:28.519
- I haven't even lit it yet.
- Oh.

00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:30.604
- Is it lit now?
- Yep.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.150
You're pathetic.

00:04:36.735 --> 00:04:40.405
Host man? Host woman?
I'm having a wonderful time!

00:04:40.489 --> 00:04:43.408
You here five hours,
and already you tear up couch,

00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:46.828
draw mustache on priceless painting,
and fill pool with brine shrimp.

00:04:46.912 --> 00:04:49.164
Not bad for a city boy, huh?

00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:53.126
By the way, I took the liberty
of fertilizing your caviar.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.223
Um... Uh...

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.061
Just relax.
I'm sure my parents will love you.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.604
You don't understand.

00:05:12.688 --> 00:05:16.400
When I get nervous,
I can't control my camouflage reflex.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.612
Oh, dear. Oh, goodness.
Oh, odds and bodkins.

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:22.823
I'll have a thorax and some feelers.

00:05:23.073 --> 00:05:24.449
You want some salad with that?

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:25.534
Yuck!

00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:28.537
Mom? Dad? You remember Kiff.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.746
This your boyfriend?

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.290
I have instant dislike of him.

00:05:31.373 --> 00:05:33.792
He too scrawny to father grandchildren.

00:05:33.959 --> 00:05:36.920
He's not scrawny. He's just small-boned.

00:05:37.004 --> 00:05:39.006
Actually, I don't have bones.

00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:42.301
I'm supported by a system
of fluid-filled bladders that...

00:05:42.384 --> 00:05:44.261
Yes, yes, you a big, squishy wuss.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.638
Amy should be dating real man. Like him!

00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:50.017
I can be manly, too.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.144
I think I'll light up a smoke.

00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:55.647
Wrong way.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.025
Smooth.

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:03.113
Look on the bright side.

00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:07.326
My parents left after you passed out,
so they didn't even see you barf.

00:06:07.409 --> 00:06:11.496
Oh, now they'll never think I'm manly
enough to date their daughter.

00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:15.334
It's okay, Kiff.

00:06:16.418 --> 00:06:18.086
I'll go get you a tissue from your tote.

00:06:19.296 --> 00:06:22.508
Hey there, Amy.
Like you to meet my buddy, Joe.

00:06:22.758 --> 00:06:23.967
Sorry I'm late.

00:06:24.051 --> 00:06:27.221
My pool game ran long at the jazz club.

00:06:27.346 --> 00:06:29.598
Kids love him.

00:06:34.436 --> 00:06:35.771
What's that weird sound?

00:06:38.565 --> 00:06:41.026
Dust storm. Dust storm!

00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:43.820
Everybody into house! Hurry before we die.

00:06:43.904 --> 00:06:45.072
And wipe your damn feet.

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:51.870
Phew. Everyone okay?
No one considering lawsuit?

00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:55.374
Hmm. I might have mental anguish.

00:06:55.457 --> 00:06:58.043
I have you know I'm friends
with every judge on planet.

00:06:58.126 --> 00:06:59.127
I'm okay, then.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:00.796
Storm dying down.

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:02.840
Leo, check if Buggalo herd is okay.

00:07:10.973 --> 00:07:12.599
What happened to the Buggalo?

00:07:12.683 --> 00:07:16.019
They been rustled under cover of storm!
We ruined!

00:07:16.395 --> 00:07:18.480
No!

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.150
Don't worry, Daddy. It'll be okay.

00:07:22.276 --> 00:07:24.152
Really? Who gonna save us?

00:07:24.361 --> 00:07:27.573
One-eye? Lobster mooch?
Drunken garbage can?

00:07:27.698 --> 00:07:29.533
This sounds like a job for...

00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:31.493
Lieutenant Kiff Kroker!

00:07:31.577 --> 00:07:32.578
All right, then.

00:07:40.669 --> 00:07:41.837
Hi-ya!

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:45.507
Those Buggalo were what made
Wong family so rich and powerful.

00:07:45.757 --> 00:07:48.719
Oh, Inez, we damn stolen! We ruined!

00:07:48.802 --> 00:07:50.262
Okay, I want a divorce.

00:07:50.345 --> 00:07:53.557
Mom! Dad! Don't ask me to choose!

00:07:53.974 --> 00:07:57.728
They're not your parents. I'm not your
sister. And that's not your golf cart.

00:07:58.145 --> 00:07:59.146
Oh.

00:08:03.108 --> 00:08:06.820
Everybody just calm down.
Kiff promised he'd catch the rustlers.

00:08:14.077 --> 00:08:17.164
Mrs. Wong, do you have a neckerchief
I could borrow?

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:22.669
My plan is to take
all the remaining Buggalo

00:08:22.753 --> 00:08:25.297
and lead them on a rough,
tough cattle drive.

00:08:25.672 --> 00:08:28.967
Then, when the rustlers attack,
I'll make a citizen’s arrest.

00:08:29.301 --> 00:08:30.552
It sounds dangerous.

00:08:30.636 --> 00:08:32.262
Someone could get killed.

00:08:32.346 --> 00:08:35.182
Fry? Leela? Bender?
I want you to go with him.

00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:36.266
Oh, man.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:37.476
"I want you to go with him."

00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:42.689
Don't worry, Mr. and Mrs. Wong,
I'll get your cattle back, or die trying.

00:08:42.773 --> 00:08:43.899
Hey, we can't lose.

00:08:43.982 --> 00:08:46.235
No, Kiff, it's too risky!

00:08:46.318 --> 00:08:48.654
You don't have to do this
to prove your manliness.

00:08:48.737 --> 00:08:49.863
Oh yes, he does!

00:08:51.406 --> 00:08:52.407
Here are your mounts.

00:08:55.244 --> 00:08:56.703
She's got a fine coat.

00:08:56.954 --> 00:08:59.873
Now, we need Buggalo to lure the rustlers.

00:08:59.957 --> 00:09:00.958
How many are left?

00:09:01.041 --> 00:09:02.167
You're lookin' at her.

00:09:02.251 --> 00:09:03.919
Betsy's the only one left.

00:09:04.002 --> 00:09:06.088
She was curled up in my hamper
when the storm hit.

00:09:06.672 --> 00:09:09.007
Oh!

00:09:09.132 --> 00:09:10.717
Aw. She likes you.

00:09:11.969 --> 00:09:16.890
Saddle up, men!
We got some no-good rustlers to catch!

00:09:25.107 --> 00:09:28.026
We got a right
To pick a little fight with rustlers

00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:31.530
Somebody wants to pick a fight with us
He'd better bite my ass!

00:09:31.655 --> 00:09:33.407
Yee-ha!

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:36.076
Wow! Look at that! Olympus Mons!

00:09:36.451 --> 00:09:38.829
The tallest volcano in the solar system.

00:09:38.912 --> 00:09:39.913
Where?

00:09:39.997 --> 00:09:40.998
Right in front of you.

00:09:41.373 --> 00:09:42.833
Oh. Oh!

00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:44.334
We'll camp near the top.

00:09:44.418 --> 00:09:46.587
The rustlers will be sure
to spot us there.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:47.671
Where?

00:09:49.006 --> 00:09:53.260
And even though the computer was off
and unplugged,

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.597
an image stayed on the screen.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:00.893
It was the Windows logo!

00:10:01.018 --> 00:10:02.853
Pss. That's not scary!

00:10:02.936 --> 00:10:04.563
It is if you're a laser printer.

00:10:04.646 --> 00:10:06.815
Okay, my turn to tell a ghost story.

00:10:07.441 --> 00:10:09.693
Once there was this woman driving.

00:10:09.776 --> 00:10:10.777
Hook on the hand!

00:10:10.986 --> 00:10:13.739
Okay, I've got one. This family...

00:10:13.822 --> 00:10:14.823
Man in the attic!

00:10:14.907 --> 00:10:18.994
Fine! Mr. Know-It-All-About-Something,
finally! You tell a story.

00:10:19.161 --> 00:10:20.162
With pleasure.

00:10:20.913 --> 00:10:23.540
Once, not far from here,

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:26.752
four people set out on a cattle drive.

00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:28.754
Robot gets bored
and kills Fry with a hammer!

00:10:29.296 --> 00:10:30.297
Sorry, go on.

00:10:30.881 --> 00:10:34.468
And then, while they sat helplessly
around the campfire,

00:10:34.551 --> 00:10:37.346
a demented, knife wielding,
escaped lunatic, libertarian,

00:10:37.429 --> 00:10:38.639
zombie, mutant snuck up and...

00:10:38.722 --> 00:10:39.848
Surprise!

00:10:42.684 --> 00:10:44.770
Amy, what are you doing here?

00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:47.022
I forgot to give you something
before you left.

00:10:47.606 --> 00:10:48.607
What?

00:10:51.944 --> 00:10:55.948
Is that your camouflage reflex,
or are you just happy to see me?

00:10:57.324 --> 00:11:00.744
I love it out here, Amy.
I feel so manly.

00:11:01.078 --> 00:11:06.583
I have a blister, I spit, and of course,
I tell no one my feelings.

00:11:06.667 --> 00:11:08.168
But you still have them, right?

00:11:08.335 --> 00:11:12.631
Oh, yes. But I keep them inside
until I can write them in my diary.

00:11:12.756 --> 00:11:15.551
It's a wonderful night.

00:11:15.634 --> 00:11:16.885
It sure is.

00:11:17.135 --> 00:11:20.806
I could just lie here beside you,
staring at the sky, all night.

00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:22.683
- I can't.
- Oh!

00:11:23.141 --> 00:11:25.269
Mmm.

00:11:28.146 --> 00:11:29.398
What's that?

00:11:29.481 --> 00:11:30.816
Maybe we just made love.

00:11:35.821 --> 00:11:38.156
The Buggalo! They're in the crater!

00:11:38.282 --> 00:11:40.826
The rustlers must have seen me coming
and run off scared!

00:11:41.326 --> 00:11:43.495
Oh, Kiff. You're so brave!

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:44.580
Shh! They'll hear us.

00:11:49.126 --> 00:11:51.044
Okay, the dynamite's in place.

00:11:51.336 --> 00:11:53.797
Are you sure there's no other way
to get the Buggalo out?

00:11:53.881 --> 00:11:57.467
Not unless your parents have thousands
of helicopters at their disposal.

00:11:57.551 --> 00:11:59.469
- Well, actually...
- Too late! This is more fun!

00:12:04.975 --> 00:12:06.768
Kiff, you did it!

00:12:07.019 --> 00:12:08.937
But how did you know
the dynamite would work?

00:12:09.021 --> 00:12:12.566
I once took a seminar in ejecting
chickens from a sand dune.

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:14.526
The principle is essentially the same.

00:12:17.279 --> 00:12:19.907
Hey, it's that
"Barbecue's Over Sound" again!

00:12:22.868 --> 00:12:24.286
Sandstorm!

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.840
We're in the eye of the storm!

00:12:36.924 --> 00:12:37.925
Where?

00:12:39.176 --> 00:12:40.219
What's that?

00:12:43.263 --> 00:12:44.723
- Oh, my gosh!
- Who are they?

00:12:45.807 --> 00:12:47.392
We are the Native Martians.

00:12:49.978 --> 00:12:52.105
Also, I didn't know Buggalo could fly.

00:12:52.189 --> 00:12:55.067
Only those who revere
Mother Mars can fly Buggalo.

00:12:55.275 --> 00:12:58.028
And only they shall have Buggalo.
And they're us.

00:12:58.111 --> 00:13:02.449
But your Martian-ness,
these Buggalo aren't yours.

00:13:02.533 --> 00:13:04.576
They belong to the Wong family.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:09.081
You mean family that took all Martian land
and gave us one lousy bead?

00:13:09.206 --> 00:13:11.625
Uh-huh. Amy Wong. And you are?

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:13.085
Mad at Wong family!

00:13:13.168 --> 00:13:15.629
We plan to ruin them by stealing Buggalo.

00:13:15.712 --> 00:13:17.589
But now we take girl instead.

00:13:18.882 --> 00:13:21.718
Wait! I'm too rich to be kidnapped!

00:13:22.511 --> 00:13:25.264
Amy! No!

00:13:28.433 --> 00:13:29.893
Don't worry, Kiff.

00:13:29.977 --> 00:13:33.689
I'm sure some other beautiful,
rich girl will fall in love with you.

00:13:51.248 --> 00:13:53.667
Hooray! You bring back cattle!

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.377
Yes. But...

00:13:55.627 --> 00:13:58.005
I'm afraid I've got some
bad news, as well.

00:13:58.088 --> 00:14:00.841
Let Amy tell us.
That way it soften the blow.

00:14:03.302 --> 00:14:04.887
Why Amy being so quiet?

00:14:05.137 --> 00:14:07.848
Um... Well... That is...

00:14:15.397 --> 00:14:17.774
Oh, no! Martians kidnap Amy!

00:14:18.942 --> 00:14:20.903
I know it them,
'cause they no use good grammar.

00:14:21.069 --> 00:14:23.572
I'll get your daughter back, sir.
I swear.

00:14:23.655 --> 00:14:24.656
Forget it, squishy.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.201
You the one lose her in first place.
You done enough.

00:14:27.326 --> 00:14:31.663
Yeah! This time we get most decorated
lawman in the whole universe!

00:14:31.788 --> 00:14:32.789
You mean...

00:14:32.956 --> 00:14:35.167
No, please, I beg you.
For the love of...

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.669
I am the man with no name.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.963
Zapp Brannigan, at your service.

00:14:41.173 --> 00:14:44.927
Please, Mr. Brannigan,
we need you go get our daughter back!

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:47.471
Very well. I'll clean up Kiff's mess.

00:14:47.554 --> 00:14:49.556
I shall go bargain
with the Martians personally.

00:14:50.849 --> 00:14:52.851
Your gasps intrigue me. Explain.

00:14:52.935 --> 00:14:54.561
Martians have no land.

00:14:54.645 --> 00:14:58.524
They been gently encouraged to live
on reservation deep underground.

00:14:58.607 --> 00:15:00.817
No one ever dare go there.

00:15:00.901 --> 00:15:02.945
This mission is incredibly dangerous!

00:15:03.028 --> 00:15:05.030
Someone's sure to be killed!

00:15:05.155 --> 00:15:07.157
Fry? Leela? Bender?

00:15:07.241 --> 00:15:09.201
Damn you, old man!

00:15:15.165 --> 00:15:18.001
Aw, look. Betsy followed you, Kiff.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:22.631
I didn't realize you were bringing
your girlfriend, Lieutenant.

00:15:24.383 --> 00:15:26.718
Oh, she won't leave me alone.

00:15:26.802 --> 00:15:28.303
Did I say girlfriend?

00:15:28.387 --> 00:15:30.347
She sounds more like a wife.

00:15:40.107 --> 00:15:42.734
Behold! The Great Stone Face of Mars!

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:46.405
Hmm. The only known entrance
to the Martian Reservation.

00:15:46.488 --> 00:15:48.407
What about the Great Stone Ass of Mars?

00:15:48.574 --> 00:15:51.201
Well yeah, but it's way on the other side
of the planet.

00:15:55.873 --> 00:15:57.291
Noseward ho!

00:16:15.934 --> 00:16:20.230
I am Singing Wind.
Chief of the Martian tribe.

00:16:20.397 --> 00:16:21.690
Take me to your leader.

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:26.153
Moving along.
Why you trespass on our land?

00:16:26.236 --> 00:16:28.655
We come to negotiate
the release of Amy Wong.

00:16:28.739 --> 00:16:33.035
And just to clarify,
land is the stuff that has sky over it.

00:16:37.998 --> 00:16:40.000
They have such respect for the planet.

00:16:40.918 --> 00:16:42.544
Cynthia used to drink Slurm.

00:16:44.505 --> 00:16:47.549
We will give back girl
when we get back planet surface.

00:16:47.633 --> 00:16:49.343
How do we even know she's alive?

00:16:49.426 --> 00:16:50.511
I'm fine.

00:16:50.594 --> 00:16:52.304
Shh. You're weakening
our bargaining position.

00:16:52.429 --> 00:16:54.473
How about, instead, you give us the girl

00:16:54.556 --> 00:16:57.518
and we carve a bunch of our Presidents
into your sacred mountain?

00:16:57.601 --> 00:16:58.727
You waste words.

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:01.355
We want return of land
that was taken from us.

00:17:01.438 --> 00:17:03.774
Actually, you traded it for a bead.

00:17:03.857 --> 00:17:06.485
Tribe suffer heap big buyer's remorse.

00:17:06.568 --> 00:17:07.611
We want land back!

00:17:07.903 --> 00:17:11.031
Chief, my people are people of law.
And that law is

00:17:11.114 --> 00:17:12.491
no backsies.

00:17:13.075 --> 00:17:15.452
The time for stupid statements is over.

00:17:20.332 --> 00:17:21.625
Oh, boy.

00:17:29.508 --> 00:17:31.552
Ow, ow, ow, ow.

00:17:31.927 --> 00:17:33.220
My eye!

00:17:43.063 --> 00:17:46.191
Ma! Pa! Our precious ranch!

00:18:00.247 --> 00:18:02.916
Amy! No! It's too windy!

00:18:09.256 --> 00:18:11.508
Stay calm, dearest! I'll save you!

00:18:13.093 --> 00:18:16.638
Kiff! You're flying Betsy

00:18:16.889 --> 00:18:17.973
Need a lift?

00:18:20.976 --> 00:18:23.812
Great Mother Mars. He has the gift.

00:18:30.527 --> 00:18:31.904
- Yay, Kiff!
- All right!

00:18:31.987 --> 00:18:35.699
Kroker, that was one
Brannigan-esque feat of heroism.

00:18:35.866 --> 00:18:37.910
We have misjudged you, green one.

00:18:37.993 --> 00:18:39.661
You fly the Buggalo like us.

00:18:39.995 --> 00:18:44.541
You have true reverence for Mother Mars.
Let there be peace between us.

00:18:44.625 --> 00:18:47.044
Yes. Let us smoke-em peace pipe.

00:18:47.419 --> 00:18:48.504
Smoke-em?

00:18:52.508 --> 00:18:53.592
Here, take.

00:18:53.842 --> 00:18:56.595
No thanks. I'm on the peace patch.

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.473
You must smoke peace pipe,
and you must do it peacefully.

00:18:59.556 --> 00:19:00.557
Or we'll kill you.

00:19:00.641 --> 00:19:03.685
Well, it's just really
that I don't feel that...

00:19:03.769 --> 00:19:05.354
Don't be such a chicken, Kiff.

00:19:05.437 --> 00:19:08.482
Teenagers all smoke,
and they seem pretty on the ball.

00:19:14.029 --> 00:19:16.240
- Yeah!
- Way to suck it!

00:19:16.323 --> 00:19:18.617
Hey, I'm smoking!

00:19:19.076 --> 00:19:20.285
I'm the greatest!

00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:27.876
Oh, monkey trumpets.

00:19:30.087 --> 00:19:32.422
You have coughed at our offer of peace.

00:19:32.506 --> 00:19:33.799
So you must die.

00:19:33.882 --> 00:19:38.595
The very bead used to crush our dreams
shall be used to crush your bones.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.764
Well actually, I don't have bones.

00:19:41.056 --> 00:19:44.726
I'm supported by a system
of fluid-filled bladders that...

00:19:48.981 --> 00:19:52.025
Wait, that's the bead
you traded your land for?

00:19:52.109 --> 00:19:53.819
It's a gigantic diamond!

00:19:53.902 --> 00:19:55.654
That thing must be worth a fortune!

00:19:55.737 --> 00:19:56.738
Really?

00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.324
Oh, phew!

00:20:05.581 --> 00:20:09.751
Oh, Chief, you've made me
the happiest girl in the world!

00:20:10.836 --> 00:20:14.214
You know, if you still want your land,
we could just trade back for it.

00:20:14.339 --> 00:20:16.925
Hmm. We always thought bead was worthless.

00:20:17.217 --> 00:20:19.219
We assumed our ancestors were cheated

00:20:19.303 --> 00:20:21.430
because they not
have concept of ownership.

00:20:21.513 --> 00:20:22.764
So we can have the diamond?

00:20:22.848 --> 00:20:25.601
No. We do have concept of ownership.

00:20:27.352 --> 00:20:28.478
You are free to go.

00:20:28.812 --> 00:20:30.898
Sorry about all the rustling
and kidnapping.

00:20:30.981 --> 00:20:32.691
But what about your sacred land?

00:20:32.774 --> 00:20:35.736
Land, schmand!
We don't want to live on this planet.

00:20:35.819 --> 00:20:39.114
It's a dump. We'll buy new planet,
and act like it's sacred.

00:20:39.364 --> 00:20:42.784
With cash like this, who's going to argue?
Nobody, that's who.

00:20:50.834 --> 00:20:53.962
Then Kiff flew Betsy,
rescued me from the tornado,

00:20:54.046 --> 00:20:55.839
and made peace with the Martians.

00:20:56.006 --> 00:20:57.925
Please, he too much of a wimp.

00:20:58.008 --> 00:21:01.595
Yeah. I'm sure it was all
Mr. Zapp Brannigan here.

00:21:01.678 --> 00:21:04.097
Please, you give me too little credit.

00:21:05.265 --> 00:21:09.228
Captain Brannigan, you're always welcome
here at Rancho Zoidberg.

00:21:11.939 --> 00:21:15.150
Money doesn't make good people.
No, siree!

00:21:19.988 --> 00:21:21.740
Thanks for saving my life, Kiff.

00:21:22.366 --> 00:21:23.492
You're my hero.

00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:25.202
Oh, you're kind.

00:21:25.577 --> 00:21:27.788
But your parents still don't like me.

00:21:27.955 --> 00:21:29.289
Well, gloviously.

00:21:29.414 --> 00:21:31.750
But if they liked you, then I wouldn't.

00:21:32.376 --> 00:21:34.002
Don't you know anything about girls?

00:21:45.931 --> 00:21:50.352
"Dear Diary.
I just made love for the second time."